  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The short answer",
      "items": [
        "People use a browser UI and customer systems call a keyed REST API",
        "other tools post signed webhooks",
        "All three paths converge on the unified intake pipeline, which writes through one DataStore port to PostgreSQL, and mail goes out through Graph"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown here",
      "items": [
        "The Notifier and mail providers, Brevo, Slack, Teams, Entra ID, the AI providers, Azure Blob and every background job",
        "They have their own diagrams",
        "Connected but out of scope: Auth.js sessions, Brevo, Slack, Microsoft Teams, Context and guards, API key service"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Constraints",
      "items": [
        "Only the DataStore port and the database blob store reach the Prisma adapter: services depend on the port so persistence swaps with one environment variable; the one recorded exception is databaseBlob.ts, which imports the Prisma client directly",
        "The browser never reaches durable state except through the API: authorization, tenant scoping and audit all live server-side"
      ]
    }
  ]
